<title>HONG KONG: Cheong Ming ends debut up at HK$1.32/shr.</title>
<headline>Cheong Ming ends debut up at HK$1.32/shr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of printing concern Cheong Ming Holdings Ltd ended their trading debut on Monday at HK$1.32, up 32 percent from their issue price of HK$1.00.</p>
<p>&quot;Trading was pretty active but buyers turned cautious after prices hit a high of HK$1.58,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Turnover was 75.45 million shares worth HK$104.6 million.</p>
<p>Cheong Ming's initial public offer of 80 million shares was 16.9 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The printing group said it would use the proceeds to buy machinery, fund the construction of a printing factory in China and for working capital.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
</text>
